OK, I'm being facetious, but poly-piling is one of the quirky things
about nethack that makes it FUN to just run around in the dungeon.
You can take an hour off just to sort through piles of stuff - anyone
here like to go to the mall and try on clothes, or look at records?
It's the same thing for me.  Without things like this, it becomes a
hack-and-slash game.  BORING.  Hell is bad enough as it is (yawn),
let's not strip all the moderately uncomplicated fun out of the game.

As far as relative character strength goes, it's not like our
characters are ever going to meet each other or anything.  The last
couple of games I played I didn't poly-pile when I got the chance.  I
just didn't feel like it.  Same goes for the ring of conflict.  Each
player gets a lot of control over how hard the game is - just walk
away from the wand of wishing if you want.

Anyway, just had to get that off my chest.  I'm less interested in
arcane combinations of class or potions and gems or new methods of
fighting (gee, we haven't had that discussion in a couple of months
:-)) than in just having fun.  Well, yes, and winning. :-)

